WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.328 --> 00:00:20.945
"Go, Whales!" Brooklyn Robbins cheered on her team in the Wayland Middle School gym.

2
00:00:20.946 --> 00:00:26.337
The basketball bounced from player to player.

3
00:00:26.338 --> 00:00:31.986
"Grab the ball, Dirk! Move!" she shouted at the team's star forward.

4
00:00:31.987 --> 00:00:38.231
Dirk raced across the court after the opposing point guard.

5
00:00:38.232 --> 00:00:47.478
Brooklyn was holding an icy water bottle. Just then it slipped from her hand and started rolling toward the court.

6
00:00:47.479 --> 00:00:53.143
She raced to get the bottle before it rolled under players' feet.

7
00:00:53.144 --> 00:00:59.165
"Here, Brooklyn." Coach Teagan grabbed the bottle and tossed it to her.

8
00:00:59.166 --> 00:01:03.893
"Thanks, Coach." Brooklyn fumbled the bottle, nearly dropping it.

9
00:01:03.894 --> 00:01:13.972
She'd gotten so caught up in watching the game that she'd forgotten to finish her task as the Whales' team manager—filling the cooler with water bottles for the players.

10
00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:19.788
Brooklyn dropped the bottle into the cooler. "Yikes," she thought.

11
00:01:19.789 --> 00:01:26.455
"If I can't handle water bottles, how will I ever handle coaching players in the professional leagues?"

12
00:01:26.456 --> 00:01:28.667
Brooklyn turned back to the game.

13
00:01:28.668 --> 00:01:36.950
Every Whales player was struggling to get the ball from the lead point guard on the Treton Terriers team.

14
00:01:36.951 --> 00:01:41.457
Brooklyn had silently nicknamed the guard "The Giant."

15
00:01:41.458 --> 00:01:49.280
Now The Giant was dribbling the ball as if he were the only player on the court.

16
00:01:49.281 --> 00:01:56.757
Dirk inched closer to The Giant. Dirk was in a perfect position for a clean shot.

17
00:01:56.758 --> 00:02:05.909
But instead of trying to steal the ball, he'd stopped moving. He looked stuck to the floor, holding his arms out like a scarecrow.

18
00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:10.074
"Coach, what's up with Dirk?" Brooklyn murmured.

19
00:02:10.075 --> 00:02:16.977
No answer. Coach was staring at his phone again. His wife was expecting triplets soon.

20
00:02:16.978 --> 00:02:21.228
"You're open, Dirk!" Brooklyn shouted. "Get the ball!"

21
00:02:21.229 --> 00:02:24.993
"Think like a Jedi!" Marv Lennox chimed in.

22
00:02:24.994 --> 00:02:32.072
Brooklyn grinned at Marv. The assistant coach scratched nervously at his gray beard.

23
00:02:32.073 --> 00:02:39.448
"Laser him!" cried another Whales player. Everyone at Wayland knew Dirk loved the Star Wars movies.

24
00:02:39.449 --> 00:02:41.972
Maybe this would get him moving.

25
00:02:41.973 --> 00:02:49.638
It didn't. The Giant sailed past Dirk and threw a shot from center court.

26
00:02:49.639 --> 00:02:56.392
The ball whisked through the hoop, and the crowd cheered.

27
00:02:56.393 --> 00:03:02.207
Brooklyn clapped. "Great three-pointer!"

28
00:03:02.208 --> 00:03:05.208
"Brooklyn, don't cheer for the enemy."

29
00:03:05.209 --> 00:03:11.287
Jacey had been sitting slumped on the sidelines after missing a free throw during the game's first quarter.

30
00:03:11.288 --> 00:03:13.879
She pulled her ponytail tighter.

31
00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:19.282
"This is a game, Jacey. There are no enemies," Brooklyn said.

32
00:03:19.283 --> 00:03:26.440
Brooklyn had known Jacey since preschool. But Jacey seemed different now that the girls were in middle school.

33
00:03:26.441 --> 00:03:31.510
She didn't text Brooklyn very often anymore or invite her to do things.

34
00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:35.367
The girls were still friends, just not close friends.

35
00:03:35.368 --> 00:03:42.012
The Whales were ten points behind when the halftime buzzer blared.

36
00:03:42.013 --> 00:03:50.497
Coach Teagan should've been rousing the tired players, but he had gone off to phone his wife.

37
00:03:50.498 --> 00:03:58.657
Marv took over trying to boost the team's morale. "You guys have to focus out there." He pointed at Stuart and Jacey.

38
00:03:58.658 --> 00:04:06.164
"The offense must push the other team's dribblers back. Dirk, use your height to jump and block whenever you can.

39
00:04:06.165 --> 00:04:12.497
Remember—this is our last regular game before play-offs start. We could use a win today."

40
00:04:12.498 --> 00:04:18.240
Brooklyn had been scooping up loose basketballs.

41
00:04:18.241 --> 00:04:26.646
When she saw the Whales' players sitting with their heads down, she jumped into the circle next to Marv—and accidentally stomped on his foot.

42
00:04:26.647 --> 00:04:29.389
"Oof!" He stumbled backward.

43
00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:33.614
"Sorry, Marv!" Brooklyn said. "I've got an idea."

44
00:04:33.615 --> 00:04:38.962
Marv rubbed his foot. "Let's hear it, Brooklyn."

45
00:04:38.963 --> 00:04:48.210
"Don't let that tall guard near the ball. He's moving better than everyone today. He dribbles . . ."

46
00:04:48.211 --> 00:04:53.207
She started to gesture with her arms, dropping all the balls she was holding.

47
00:04:53.208 --> 00:05:00.864
Dirk burst out laughing. "Everyone moves better than you, klutz!"

48
00:05:00.865 --> 00:05:04.281
Jacey and a few other players laughed too.

49
00:05:04.282 --> 00:05:09.765
"I'm graceful inside!" Brooklyn said quickly, forcing a smile.

50
00:05:09.766 --> 00:05:17.923
Marv was frowning. "Dirk, apologize to Brooklyn." There was a long silence.

51
00:05:17.924 --> 00:05:21.151
"Now!" the assistant coach said.

52
00:05:21.152 --> 00:05:24.113
"Sorry," Dirk mumbled.

53
00:05:24.114 --> 00:05:29.766
"Thank you," Marv said. "And thanks for the tip on that guard, Brooklyn."

54
00:05:29.767 --> 00:05:35.750
Brooklyn nodded. "Don't let Dirk's insult get to you," she told herself.

55
00:05:35.751 --> 00:05:43.757
At basketball camp last year, her counselor had said, "Some players are big, some small, some fast, some slow.

56
00:05:43.758 --> 00:05:47.899
But if you play smart, you can score hoops against anyone."

57
00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:57.902
It had taken time for Brooklyn to understand what her counselor meant, especially with bullies calling her "clumsy oaf" or "klutz" throughout elementary school.

58
00:05:57.903 --> 00:06:03.823
Since arriving at Wayland Middle School for sixth grade, Brooklyn had lived for basketball.

59
00:06:03.824 --> 00:06:10.051
Making the Whales team was nearly impossible, with the way she moved and her small size.

60
00:06:10.052 --> 00:06:17.899
But working as the Whales' team manager was her first step to achieving her dream of becoming a coach one day.

61
00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:25.213
After halftime the Terriers quickly scored another three-pointer.

62
00:06:25.213 --> 00:06:29.301
Marv and Coach Teagan called the Whales in for a time-out.

63
00:06:29.302 --> 00:06:37.721
Brooklyn tugged on Marv's sleeve. "What about that special play I showed everyone in practice last week? The loop play?"

64
00:06:37.722 --> 00:06:40.636
Dirk scowled. "Dumb play."

65
00:06:40.637 --> 00:06:44.459
"Dirk!" Coach Teagan looked up from texting.

66
00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:49.038
"This is your last warning to be respectful." He turned to the team.

67
00:06:49.039 --> 00:06:52.530
"Brooklyn's idea is good. We've got to mix it up."

68
00:06:52.531 --> 00:06:57.591
Dirk nodded and mumbled another apology, but he was still scowling.

69
00:06:57.592 --> 00:07:05.013
Coach Teagan put one hand out and each player layered a hand on top for the team cheer.

70
00:07:05.014 --> 00:07:09.153
"Whales Whoosh!" they shouted.

71
00:07:09.154 --> 00:07:13.495
The Whales' first try with the loop play failed.

72
00:07:13.496 --> 00:07:21.051
"Foul!" The official pointed at Dirk. He'd slammed into his giant opponent.

73
00:07:21.052 --> 00:07:24.681
"Play smart, Dirk!" Brooklyn shouted.

74
00:07:24.682 --> 00:07:32.655
A Whales player dribbled and passed the ball to Dirk. The team was trying the loop play again.

75
00:07:32.656 --> 00:07:43.729
Brooklyn ran down the sidelines. "Go, Dirk!" She bumped into someone near the team bench. It was Jacey.

76
00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:46.027
"Sorry," Brooklyn said.

77
00:07:46.028 --> 00:07:52.869
"It's okay." Jacey moved in front of Brooklyn. "Yeah, Dirk!"

78
00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:57.726
Brooklyn saw Dirk was now midcourt, with a clear shot to the basket.

79
00:07:57.727 --> 00:08:01.141
"Shoot it! You've got this!" Marv yelled.

80
00:08:01.142 --> 00:08:11.349
Dirk raced across the court, dribbling. Suddenly The Giant lunged for the ball.

81
00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:14.787
"Loop it!" Brooklyn called.

82
00:08:14.789 --> 00:08:23.446
Dirk looked up. Brooklyn hoped he'd heard her, but the crowd was loud—really loud.

83
00:08:23.447 --> 00:08:27.431
"Loop! Loop!" Marv and Coach shouted.

84
00:08:27.432 --> 00:08:35.424
Dirk turned, but he went the wrong direction, toward the other team's basket.

85
00:08:35.425 --> 00:08:42.086
"Go left, Dirk!" Brooklyn flung out her arms, accidentally whacking Jacey.

86
00:08:42.087 --> 00:08:44.603
"Ow!" Jacey cried.

87
00:08:44.604 --> 00:08:46.259
"Sorry, Jacey! I—"

88
00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:51.834
Just then Dirk swiveled sideways with the basketball.

89
00:08:51.835 --> 00:08:59.275
Unable to weave through the players blocking center court, he bolted down the sideline.

90
00:08:59.276 --> 00:09:05.084
The Giant lunged for the ball again, slamming into Dirk.

91
00:09:05.085 --> 00:09:14.817
The buzzer blared. The game was over, but Dirk was still moving, and moving too fast to stop.

92
00:09:14.818 --> 00:09:27.926
He stumbled off the court—and crashed straight into Brooklyn.
